---
import ResearchPage from '../../layouts/ResearchPage.astro';
import { research, fingerprint } from '../../data/keyword-research.js';
import { FIT, CLUSTERS, INTENTS, filterRows, sortRows } from '../../lib/keyword-analysis.js';
const { rows, audit, months } = research;
const fmt = (n) => n == null ? '—' : new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US').format(n);
const percent = (n, raw) => n == null ? (raw.includes('∞') ? '∞ · no finite baseline' : '—') : `${n > 0 ? '+' : ''}${n}%`;
const candidates = filterRows(rows, { fit: 'candidates' });
const initial = sortRows(candidates).slice(0,25);
const selected = rows.find(r => r.keyword === 'đánh giá google maps');
const counts = Object.keys(FIT).map(key => ({ key, count: rows.filter(r => r.fit === key).length }));
const clusters = Object.entries(CLUSTERS).map(([key, label]) => ({ key, label, count: rows.filter(r => r.cluster === key).length, candidateCount: candidates.filter(r => r.cluster === key).length }));
const payload = JSON.stringify(research).replace(/</g, '\\u003c').replace(/>/g, '\\u003e').replace(/&/g, '\\u0026');
const reviewTerm = rows.find(r => r.keyword === 'đánh giá google maps');
const setupTerm = rows.find(r => r.keyword === 'cách tạo google map cho doanh nghiệp');
const websiteMentions = rows.filter(r => /\bwebsite\b/i.test(r.keyword)).length;
const qrMentions = rows.filter(r => /\bqr\b/i.test(r.keyword)).length;
const points = selected.monthly.map((v,i) => `${45+i*610/11},${195-(v??0)/Math.max(1,...selected.monthly.filter(v=>v!==null))*145}`).join(' ');
---
<ResearchPage>
  <div class="research-shell">
    <aside class="research-sidebar" aria-label="Research navigation">
      <a class="brand research-brand" href="/" aria-label="Lumi Local homepage"><img src="/brand/lumi-logo.svg" width="34" height="34" alt="" /><span>Lumi <strong>Local</strong></span></a>
      <p class="sidebar-label">RESEARCH / 01</p>
      <nav>
        <a href="#overview"><span class="nav-index">01</span> Overview</a>
        <a href="#explorer"><span class="nav-index">02</span> Keyword explorer</a>
        <a href="#strategy"><span class="nav-index">03</span> Next decisions</a>
        <a href="#methodology"><span class="nav-index">04</span> Method & sources</a>
      </nav>
      <div class="sidebar-foot"><span class="status-dot"></span> Historical snapshot<p>Sep 2025 — Aug 2026<br />Vietnamese keywords · VND<br />Target location unknown</p><a href="/data/keywords.csv" download>Download source CSV ↗</a></div>
    </aside>
    <div class="research-content">
      <header class="research-topbar"><span>Intelligence desk <span class="topbar-divider">/</span> Keyword research</span><a href="/">View Lumi Local ↗</a><form method="post" action="/data/logout"><button class="research-signout" type="submit">Sign out</button></form></header>
      <main id="main">
        <section id="overview" class="overview">
          <div class="research-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">LUMI LOCAL · SEARCH INTELLIGENCE</p><h1>Find the demand<br /> worth pursuing.</h1></div><div class="heading-note"><span class="snapshot-label">CSV evidence / human judgment</span><p>Search interest is a starting point. Offer fit, buyer intent and paid feedback decide what deserves your time.</p><a class="text-link" href="#explorer">Explore the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div>
          <div class="kpi-grid">
            <article class="kpi"><span>Unique keyword terms</span><strong>{fmt(audit.uniqueRows)}</strong><small>From {fmt(audit.rawRows)} source rows</small></article>
            <article class="kpi"><span>Content candidates <sup>†</sup></span><strong>{fmt(candidates.length)}</strong><small>{fmt(counts[0].count)} offer-adjacent · {fmt(counts[1].count)} educational</small></article>
            <article class="kpi"><span>Exact duplicates removed</span><strong>{fmt(audit.duplicateCount)}</strong><small>{audit.conflictCount} conflicting duplicate records</small></article>
            <article class="kpi"><span>Organic observations</span><strong>{audit.organicObservations}</strong><small>Rankings and traffic are unknown</small></article>
          </div>
          <p class="metric-footnote">† Rule-based research candidates, not validated buyers or ranking opportunities. Similar variants remain separate; search estimates may overlap.</p>
          <div class="overview-grid">
            <section class="evidence-sheet fit-sheet" aria-labelledby="fit-title"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / OFFER FIT</p><h2 id="fit-title">The useful slice is small.</h2></div><span class="small-meta">Unique terms</span></div>
              <div class="fit-rail" aria-hidden="true">{counts.map(({key,count})=><span class={`rail-${key}`} style={`flex:${count}`}></span>)}</div>
              <div class="fit-list">{counts.map(({key,count})=><a href="#explorer" data-fit-preset={key}><span><i class={`fit-dot dot-${key}`}></i>{FIT[key].label}</span><strong>{fmt(count)}<small>{(100*count/rows.length).toFixed(1)}%</small></strong></a>)}</div>
              <p class="small-meta">Click a category to inspect its terms. Classification is an analyst hypothesis.</p>
            </section>
            <section class="evidence-sheet insight-sheet"><p class="eyebrow">STRATEGIC READING · INFERENCE</p><h2>Maps demand is not<br /> package demand.</h2><p>The largest terms are navigation queries. Verification and Maps SEO searches often request services outside Lumi Local’s scope.</p><div class="insight-bottom"><strong>{websiteMentions} terms mention “website”. {qrMentions} mention “QR”.</strong><p>The sampled website terms describe Maps embedding and look mostly technical/DIY. They may help an owner, but do not yet validate demand for Lumi’s owner-confirmed directions link.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="#strategy">Turn this into a test ↗</a></section>
          </div>
          <section class="evidence-sheet cluster-sheet" aria-labelledby="cluster-title"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / TOPIC COVERAGE</p><h2 id="cluster-title">What the file actually covers</h2></div><span class="small-meta">Counts, not additive search demand</span></div>
            <div class="cluster-grid">{clusters.map(cluster=><button type="button" data-cluster-preset={cluster.key} class="cluster-row"><span>{cluster.label}</span><div class="cluster-track"><i style={`width:${Math.max(1,100*cluster.count/Math.max(...clusters.map(c=>c.count)))}%`}></i></div><strong>{fmt(cluster.count)}</strong><small>{cluster.candidateCount ? `${cluster.candidateCount} candidates` : 'No candidates'}</small></button>)}</div>
          </section>
        </section>
        <section id="explorer" class="explorer">
          <div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / KEYWORD EXPLORER</p><h2>From terms to decisions.</h2><p>Search without accents. Select a keyword to inspect its history and classification.</p></div><button type="button" id="export-csv" class="button button-secondary" disabled>Export filtered CSV ↗</button></div>
          <noscript><p class="notice">JavaScript is off. The first 25 candidates and source download remain available. Filters, selection and export require JavaScript.</p></noscript>
          <form id="keyword-filters" class="evidence-sheet filter-bar">
            <label class="search-field">Search keywords<input type="search" name="query" placeholder="Try: đánh giá, doanh nghiệp…" autocomplete="off" /></label>
            <label>Offer fit<select name="fit"><option value="candidates" selected>Content candidates</option><option value="all">All terms</option>{Object.entries(FIT).map(([key,item])=><option value={key}>{item.label}</option>)}</select></label>
            <label>Topic<select name="cluster"><option value="all">All topics</option>{Object.entries(CLUSTERS).map(([key,label])=><option value={key}>{label}</option>)}</select></label>
            <label>Intent <span class="small-meta">(inferred)</span><select name="intent"><option value="all">All intents</option>{Object.entries(INTENTS).map(([key,label])=><option value={key}>{label}</option>)}</select></label>
            <label>Min. searches<input type="number" name="minVolume" min="0" step="1" value="0" /></label>
            <label>Sort by<select name="sort"><option value="score">Editorial priority ↓</option><option value="volume">Monthly searches ↓</option><option value="change">3-month change ↓</option><option value="yoy">YoY change ↓</option><option value="adCompetition">Ad competition ↑</option></select></label>
            <button type="reset" class="reset-button">Reset filters</button>
          </form>
          <div class="results-strip"><p id="result-summary" role="status" aria-live="polite">{fmt(candidates.length)} matching terms · {fmt(audit.uniqueRows)} total</p><p>Estimates in CSV · no live feed</p></div>
          <div class="evidence-sheet keyword-table-sheet"><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Keyword results, horizontally scrollable" tabindex="0"><table><caption class="sr-only">Keyword estimates and inferred fit. Competition is advertising competition, not SEO difficulty.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Keyword / topic</th><th scope="col">Offer fit <sup>†</sup></th><th scope="col">Searches / mo.</th><th scope="col">3-mo. change</th><th scope="col">Ad index</th><th scope="col">Priority <sup>†</sup></th></tr></thead><tbody id="keyword-rows">{initial.map(row=><tr class={row.id===selected.id?'selected-row':''}><td><button type="button" class="keyword-select" data-keyword-id={row.id} aria-pressed={row.id===selected.id}><span lang="vi">{row.keyword}</span></button><small>{CLUSTERS[row.cluster]}</small></td><td><span class={`fit-tag tag-${row.fit}`}>{FIT[row.fit].label}</span></td><td>{fmt(row.volume)}</td><td>{percent(row.change,row.changeRaw)}</td><td>{fmt(row.adCompetition)}</td><td><strong class="score-value">{row.score}</strong><span class="small-meta"> / 100</span></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
            <div class="pagination"><span id="page-summary">1–{initial.length} of {candidates.length}</span><label>Rows<select id="page-size"><option value="25">25</option><option value="50">50</option><option value="100">100</option></select></label><div><button type="button" id="previous-page" disabled aria-label="Previous results page">←</button><button type="button" id="next-page" disabled aria-label="Next results page">→</button></div></div>
          </div>
          <details id="export-receipt" class="evidence-sheet export-receipt" hidden>
            <summary id="export-summary">CSV export ready</summary>
            <a id="csv-download" class="text-link" download="LumiLocal-keywords-filtered.csv">Download filtered CSV ↗</a>
            <p class="small-meta">If your browser blocks the download, you can select and save the CSV text below.</p>
            <label for="csv-preview" class="sr-only">Generated filtered CSV</label>
            <textarea id="csv-preview" readonly rows="6" spellcheck="false"></textarea>
          </details>
          <p class="metric-footnote">† Fit, intent and priority are explainable rules, not measured SEO difficulty. “∞” has no finite baseline; missing values stay unknown. <a href="#methodology">See the method ↗</a></p>
          <section id="keyword-detail" class="evidence-sheet detail-sheet" aria-labelledby="detail-keyword"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">SELECTED KEYWORD · SOURCE HISTORY</p><h3 id="detail-keyword" lang="vi">{selected.keyword}</h3></div><span id="detail-confidence" class="confidence-label">{selected.confidence} classification confidence</span></div>
            <div class="detail-grid"><div><div class="trend-head"><strong id="detail-volume">{fmt(selected.volume)}<small> avg. monthly searches</small></strong><span id="detail-yoy">YoY {percent(selected.yoy,selected.yoyRaw)}</span></div><div id="trend-chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 700 240" role="img" aria-label={`Monthly estimated searches for ${selected.keyword}. ${months[0]} to ${months[11]}.`}><line x1="45" y1="195" x2="655" y2="195" class="chart-grid" /><polyline points={points} class="trend-line" />{selected.monthly.map((v,i)=><circle cx={45+i*610/11} cy={195-(v??0)/Math.max(1,...selected.monthly.filter(v=>v!==null))*145} r="4" class="trend-point"><title>{months[i]}: {fmt(v)}</title></circle>)}<text x="45" y="225">Sep 2025</text><text x="655" y="225" text-anchor="end">Aug 2026</text></svg></div><details class="monthly-values"><summary>Read all 12 monthly estimates</summary><dl id="monthly-values">{months.map((month,i)=><div><dt>{month}</dt><dd>{fmt(selected.monthly[i])}</dd></div>)}</dl></details></div>
              <div class="detail-reading"><p class="eyebrow">WHY THIS CLASSIFICATION</p><p id="detail-reason">{selected.reason}</p><dl><div><dt>Inferred intent</dt><dd id="detail-intent">{INTENTS[selected.intent]}</dd></div><div><dt>Top-of-page bid range</dt><dd id="detail-bids">{selected.bidLow===null ? 'Unknown' : `${fmt(selected.bidLow)}–${fmt(selected.bidHigh)} VND`}</dd></div><div><dt>CSV occurrences</dt><dd id="detail-occurrences">{selected.occurrences}</dd></div></dl><p class="small-meta">Bids are historical advertising estimates. They do not establish a current CPC, acquisition cost or willingness to buy Lumi Local.</p></div>
            </div>
          </section>
        </section>
        <section id="strategy" class="strategy-section">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / NEXT DECISIONS · RECOMMENDATIONS</p><h2>Prove the buyer bridge.<br />Then expand.</h2><p class="strategy-intro">Strongest objection: a person looking for a map or leaving a review may never buy a presence package. The CSV is historical and has no organic observations. Search interest, owner pain and paid demand remain separate evidence.</p>
          <div class="strategy-grid"><article><span class="strategy-number">01</span><h3>Measure the published honest-review guide</h3><p lang="vi">“Cách tạo mã QR để khách chia sẻ trải nghiệm trên Google”</p><p>Seed: <span lang="vi">{reviewTerm.keyword}</span> · <strong>{fmt(reviewTerm.volume)}/mo.</strong> in the Sep 2025–Aug 2026 export. This mixed consumer/owner term is not proof of review-service demand. The bilingual guide is already published.</p><p class="strategy-action">Next: read dated Search Console page/query data when available. Owner feedback remains uncollected; test with 10 reachable owners only through an explicitly authorized channel. Continue if ≥3 describe a recent relevant problem and ≥2 request a package preview; otherwise revise or stop. These are proposed thresholds, not results.</p></article>
            <article><span class="strategy-number">02</span><h3>Keep directions inside the existing guide</h3><p lang="vi">“Thêm chỉ đường Google Maps vào website dịch vụ”</p><p>Seed: <span lang="vi">tích hợp google map vào website</span> · <strong>10/mo.</strong> in the historical export; targeting is unknown. A 7 October Google sample found overlapping how-to results for embed variants and mixed directions/profile-setup intent. The existing VI/EN guide now links Google’s official share-link steps. This sample supports answering the question in the existing guide, not adding a new page.</p><p class="strategy-action">Next: inspect page-level indexing/discovery once on or after 14 October. Reconsider a new page only if owner-language evidence and qualified enquiries support it. A successful live fetch is not proof of indexing or buyer intent.</p></article>
            <article><span class="strategy-number">03</span><h3>Repair the research coverage</h3><p>Website, QR and local-owner language are barely represented in this Maps-heavy export.</p><p>Use <span lang="vi">{setupTerm.keyword}</span> (<strong>{fmt(setupTerm.volume)}/mo.</strong>) as an educational bridge, not a managed-profile service. Expand with owner phrases for service menus, Call/Zalo and package setup.</p><p class="strategy-action">Test: export 20 additional buyer-language seeds with location, network and date settings recorded. Keep unmeasured phrases separate. Stop claiming market coverage until all 3 presence pillars are represented.</p></article>
          </div>
          <div class="strategy-tradeoff"><div><h3>Protect the sales experiment.</h3><p>One guide trades reach for a clearer audience. Low-intent traffic can increase support load and pull delivery into excluded Google work. Content is a reversible test; scaling sales is a separate decision.</p></div><div><span class="strategy-gate">REPOSITORY PILOT GATE · NOT AN SEO FORECAST</span><p>30 qualified businesses → ≥6 paid signals, including ≥2 paid Starter purchases; average preview time ≤5 minutes. Contribution and standardized delivery gates still apply before expanding headcount.</p></div></div>
          <p class="strategy-footer">Confidence: moderate in the scope distinction; low in demand and conversion. These thresholds are proposed test rules, except the existing 30-business repository pilot gate. One disclosed Reddit comment is logged separately; no owner interviews, attributable enquiries, paid signals or ad spend are recorded here.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="methodology" class="method-section"><div class="section-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / METHOD & SOURCES</p><h2>Evidence you can inspect.</h2><p>Source metrics are facts about this export. Classification and decisions are hypotheses.</p></div><a class="button button-secondary" href="/data/keywords.csv" download>Original CSV ↗</a></div>
          <div class="method-grid"><article class="evidence-sheet"><h3>Data quality receipt</h3><dl class="audit-list"><div><dt>History window</dt><dd>{months[0]} – {months.at(-1)}</dd></div><div><dt>Missing bid ranges</dt><dd>{fmt(audit.missingBids)} / {fmt(rows.length)}</dd></div><div><dt>Missing ad indexes</dt><dd>{audit.missingCompetition} / {fmt(rows.length)}</dd></div><div><dt>Terms with infinite changes</dt><dd>{audit.nonFiniteChanges}</dd></div><div><dt>Accent/spacing variant groups</dt><dd>{audit.normalizedVariantGroups} · kept separate</dd></div><div><dt>Exported targeting / extraction date</dt><dd>Not supplied</dd></div><div><dt>Analysis rules reviewed</dt><dd>7 October 2026</dd></div></dl><p class="small-meta">Exact keyword duplicates keep the first source record. There are no conflicting values in this file. Similar phrases may share close-variant estimates; volume is never summed as unique demand.</p><p class="fingerprint">SOURCE SHA-256<br /><code>{fingerprint}</code></p></article>
          <article class="evidence-sheet"><h3>Priority is an editorial rule.</h3><p>Offer-adjacent = 60 fit points; educational bridge = 40. Add intent points (informational 10, commercial 20, transactional 25, navigational 0) and a capped logarithmic demand term:</p><code class="formula">15 × min(1, log10(1 + searches) / 4)</code><p>Round to a whole number. Outside-offer and excluded terms score 0. The rule deliberately favors fit over raw volume; it is not trained, calibrated or a probability of ranking.</p><p>Keyword wording assigns topic, fit and intent. Confidence refers to this classification only. Three bounded Google query samples were reviewed on 7 October; they do not provide a complete SERP audit, difficulty score or buyer-intent validation.</p><p class="small-meta">Missing values are null, zero is preserved, and infinite changes are displayed without invented percentages. Supplied average searches and the monthly series are kept as separate source metrics.</p></article>
          </div>
          <div class="source-notes"><h3>Primary references</h3><p>Definitions and policy checked 6 October 2026.</p><ol><li><a href="https://support.google.com/google-ads/answer/3022575?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads: historical keyword metrics ↗</a><p>Average searches include close variants and depend on export settings. Competition counts advertisers; it is not organic difficulty. Rounded estimates and overlapping variants limit aggregation.</p></li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/business/answer/16816815?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Business Profile: review links and QR codes ↗</a><p>Owners can share a review link or QR. Lumi’s role remains the agreed artwork and setup; Google account ownership stays with the owner.</p></li><li><a href="https://support.google.com/contributionpolicy/answer/7400114?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Maps: prohibited and restricted contributions ↗</a><p>Invite genuine experiences. Do not buy, incentivize or gate reviews, or request a rating.</p></li></ol><p class="small-meta">This workspace requires server-side sign-in, including its source CSV. “Noindex” also requests search exclusion. No Search Console, live rankings, paid outcomes or current market targeting are connected.</p></div>
        </section>
        <footer class="research-footer"><span>Lumi Local / Research workspace</span><a href="#overview">Back to overview ↑</a></footer>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script is:inline type="application/json" id="keyword-dataset" set:html={payload}></script>
  <script>
    import '../../scripts/keyword-dashboard.js';
  </script>
</ResearchPage>
